# UseCase Pattern

```kotlin
// List use case — implements UseCase<T> interface
@Inject
class Get{Items}UseCase(
    private val repository: {Feature}Repository
) : UseCase<List<{Entity}>> {
    override operator fun invoke(): Flow<Result<List<{Entity}>>> {
        return repository.get{Items}()
    }
}

// Single-item / action use case — standalone class
@Inject
class Get{Item}ByIdUseCase(
    private val repository: {Feature}Repository
) {
    suspend operator fun invoke(id: String): Result<{Entity}> {
        return repository.get{Item}ById(id)
    }
}

// Create/Update/Delete use case
@Inject
class Create{Item}UseCase(
    private val repository: {Feature}Repository
) {
    suspend operator fun invoke(entity: {Entity}): Result<{Entity}> {
        return repository.create{Item}(entity)
    }
}
```

## Rules
- One use case per action (Single Responsibility)
- `@Inject` on class
- `operator fun invoke()` — enables `useCase()` call syntax
- List fetches return `Flow<Result<List<T>>>`, mutations return `suspend Result<T>`
- Use cases only depend on repository interfaces, never on data-layer classes
- All use cases in `domain/usecase/{feature}/` directory
